{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177363-advice-on-how-to-make-a-sadistic-wrestilng-promoter-a-good-villain-for-changelings","id":1177363,"title":"Advice on how to make a sadistic wrestilng promoter a good villain for Changelings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-19T10:52:28-08:00","id":1177363,"title":"Advice on how to make a sadistic wrestilng promoter a good villain for Changelings","content":"I am thinking up villain for a Changeling chronicle I want to do someday and one of them is a pro-wrestling promoter named Howard Thorne. Mr. Thorne runs a wrestling company called North American Extreme Wrestling or NAEW. Thorne labels his brand the most brutal in the country, especially when it comes to Hardcore matches where stuff like barbed wire and pool sticks are used. Mr. Thorne himself is incredibly sadistic and loves to watch the pain on the faces of his wrestlers as they fight. In fact, he sometimes wrestles himself and brings out as much pain to his opponents as his network would allow before finishing them with a pin. My question is how could this guy, who is a human. be a good antagonist for a motley of Changelings to fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T12:36:32-08:00","id":1177388,"title":"","content":"So why is this guy human? Honest question. As a human, it doesn't sound like he's doing much that would raise the attention of most Kithain. Is dude an asshole? Sure. Is he doing anything to destroy glamour or promote banality? Eh, not really. Unless he's doing something that directly messes with your PCs' interests, I don't know why they'd care. If anything, he might be making it easier for changelings of certain tastes to find dreamers.<br /> <br /> He might even *be* some changeling's dreamer and the NAEW is the result of that musing \u2014 which could be some good story fodder. In that case though, he's probably not the main bad guy, but lever your PCs could use to apply pressure to his changeling patron.<br /> <br /> Back to my original question, you have a pretty classic set up for a thallain or a dauntain. That would get just about any Kithain interested. Regardless of personal connections, he'd be an existential threat to all changelings. Why not go that route?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 01-19-2018, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T12:41:19-08:00","id":1177390,"title":"","content":"You make a good point. I can see a ogre being sadistic toward pro wrestlers. In fact, a Ogre would make be better at causing pain then a human. The only flaw is that most Ogres are not business savy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-19-2018, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T13:17:38-08:00","id":1177396,"title":"","content":"Maybe the ogre is the face and someone else, say a boggart or a sevatal, is running the business side behind the scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T13:37:33-08:00","id":1177398,"title":"","content":"A Boggart and a Ogre doing this a way to both get Glamour and feed their cruel urges. One idea i have is that the two force the PCs to fight their number one wrestler, Balor the Terrible, in a hardcore match in a PPV match. The twist is that Balor is human and well,the Mists will not let you use magic against him with 1000s of people watching you. Plus, the Ogre instructed him to break the PCs. If their is a troll pc, he is forced to watch while tied up backstage. Also, if a Sidhe is part of the group, he is forced to fight Balor by himself due to the Boggart hating Sidhes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T17:51:41-08:00","id":1177466,"title":"","content":"Besides Trolls, i wonder which Kith would be best for fighting against a pro wrestler?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T19:44:52-08:00","id":1177494,"title":"","content":"Redcaps would be second best at fighting a wrestler. Intimidation (real or via acting) is a thing in wrestling.<br /> <br /> If you want a fighty challenge around this guy you could also add in nightmares and stuff. This guy sounds like he'd be inspiring quite a few, especially among kids who tuned in to see wrestling and got sadistic business. One way to &quot;win&quot; could be to play &quot;good guy&quot; wrestlers who beat the &quot;bad guys&quot; on TV. There's also the possibility of a story hook drawing them in. What if a relative of a PC or someone they know gets suckered into trying out for this guy, thinking it's all fake?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23656-lanir","name":"Lanir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T19:51:24-08:00","id":1177496,"title":"","content":"The Ogre giving children nightmares would be a great idea. Perhaps both Balor The Terrible and the Ogre are fighting the PCs in the hardcore match while the Boggart is watching sadistically from his office. Now i should determine how the PCs could defeat Balor The Terrible, since he is a human and not a Thallian, unlike his partner Thorne. Plus, he is not Enchanted, so using Cantrips are out, especially in a crowded stadium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-19-2018, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T12:29:12-08:00","id":1177658,"title":"","content":"How much Glamour would Pro Wrestling generate for Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T11:46:57-08:00","id":1177901,"title":"","content":"Well the whole set up, would explain why the Ultimate Warrior spent his whole career in bedlam...<br /> LOADING UP THE SPACE SHIP WITH DA ROCKET FUEL! LOAD IT WITH THE WORDS OF THE WARRRIIOR! HUAK HOGAN! *skronk*<br /> Yeah, that guy has very little banality. And he is a poet. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/74HP7EPywXY?t=1m16s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/74HP7EPywXY?t=1m16s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/74HP7EPywXY?t=1m16s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/74HP7EPywXY?t=1m16s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T20:28:48-08:00","id":1177989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177363-advice-on-how-to-make-a-sadistic-wrestilng-promoter-a-good-villain-for-changelings?p=1177658#post1177658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Glamour would Pro Wrestling generate for Changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure to be honest. It would be a matter of deciding how many people were really inspiried rather than just somewhat entertained. It also seems like it would have to do with how connected the changelings were to the audience because it seems a sort of Reverie. I think usually big public things like that tend to generate dross more than glamour though, or maybe power a freehold nearby. Someone may think of a better response though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23656-lanir","name":"Lanir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T20:37:25-08:00","id":1177990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177363-advice-on-how-to-make-a-sadistic-wrestilng-promoter-a-good-villain-for-changelings?p=1177388#post1177388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why is this guy human? Honest question. As a human, it doesn't sound like he's doing much that would raise the attention of most Kithain. Is dude an asshole? Sure. Is he doing anything to destroy glamour or promote banality? Eh, not really. Unless he's doing something that directly messes with your PCs' interests, I don't know why they'd care. If anything, he might be making it easier for changelings of certain tastes to find dreamers.<br /> <br /> He might even *be* some changeling's dreamer and the NAEW is the result of that musing \u2014 which could be some good story fodder. In that case though, he's probably not the main bad guy, but lever your PCs could use to apply pressure to his changeling patron.<br /> <br /> Back to my original question, you have a pretty classic set up for a thallain or a dauntain. That would get just about any Kithain interested. Regardless of personal connections, he'd be an existential threat to all changelings. Why not go that route?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Meh, I could see him drawing the attention of players who style themselves as valorous heroes who wish to put an end to his barbaric blood sport. Even more so if some of his fighters aren't exactly competing of their own free will.<br /> <br /> As for which kith might be good at fighting him, I've seen Troll and Redcap already suggested, but I'd also like to suggest using a Satyr.<br /> <br /> <br /> More than anything else, Satyrs are wild and passionate. And really, what could be more wild and passionate than beating the daylights out of somebody in front of a crowd of 1,000 rabid, cheering spectators? The Troll might take part because he's obligated, the Redcap might take part because he's bloodthirsty. The Satyr would take part because the people came for a show, and they plan to give them one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T08:11:52-08:00","id":1178077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177363-advice-on-how-to-make-a-sadistic-wrestilng-promoter-a-good-villain-for-changelings?p=1177990#post1177990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Meh, I could see him drawing the attention of players who style themselves as valorous heroes who wish to put an end to his barbaric blood sport. Even more so if some of his fighters aren't exactly competing of their own free will.<br /> <br /> As for which kith might be good at fighting him, I've seen Troll and Redcap already suggested, but I'd also like to suggest using a Satyr.<br /> <br /> <br /> More than anything else, Satyrs are wild and passionate. And really, what could be more wild and passionate than beating the daylights out of somebody in front of a crowd of 1,000 rabid, cheering spectators? The Troll might take part because he's obligated, the Redcap might take part because he's bloodthirsty. The Satyr would take part because the people came for a show, and they plan to give them one!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA Satyr using the crowd's cheers and jeers as a source of glamour sounds awesome. Besides the Ogre and Balor the Terrible, I am considering including Balor's manager in this fight. Not as a opponent mind you, but as a obstacle. Because, like all Heel managers, once he sees that his client is about to lose, he is going to do anything in his power to turn that around, even attack the Pcs himself. Mostly by sneak attacking them with a pool stick all the way to interrupting a jump from the turnbuckle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T06:46:40-08:00","id":1181381,"title":"","content":"What if some of the participants aren't exactly willing? You could have a chronicle where some Kithain gets kidnapped off the street (either a &quot;high value&quot; princess or a common friend or something like that), and eventually shows up in a &quot;Hardcore&quot; match. Eventually it becomes clear that if the person doesn't fight, they will &quot;suffer a serious injury, causing them to retire to someplace where they will never be found.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe the Promoter is even some sort of &quot;hunter&quot;. A mortal who stumbled upon the notes of another hunter and was able to use those notes to identify certain supernaturals and manipulate them into getting into the ring. (He doesn't tell anyone this of course, somebody might try to muscle in on his racket). Perhaps he's drugged some of them, offered some vampires a free and easy source of blood, paid them, threatened their loved ones or whatever. Also keep in mind that this guy has some lore, but he's got no way of knowing for sure that the people he's throwing into the ring are actually supernatural. Chances are some humans have died because of this guy (after they signed wavers of course.. nobody fights without a waver.. but EVERYBODY fights.)<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the more this guy keeps it up, the more he learns. The more he learns, the more dangerous he is. He might even have other Hunters supporting him from the shadows so they can try to learn more themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T20:51:55-07:00","id":1263159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177363-advice-on-how-to-make-a-sadistic-wrestilng-promoter-a-good-villain-for-changelings#post1177363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thinking up villain for a Changeling chronicle I want to do someday and one of them is a pro-wrestling promoter named Howard Thorne. Mr. Thorne runs a wrestling company called North American Extreme Wrestling or NAEW. Thorne labels his brand the most brutal in the country, especially when it comes to Hardcore matches where stuff like barbed wire and pool sticks are used. Mr. Thorne himself is incredibly sadistic and loves to watch the pain on the faces of his wrestlers as they fight. In fact, he sometimes wrestles himself and brings out as much pain to his opponents as his network would allow before finishing them with a pin. My question is how could this guy, who is a human. be a good antagonist for a motley of Changelings to fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that I'm a little late and don't know C:tD very well but maybe it will help you: <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Extreme_Wrestling_Warfare\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ex...stling_Warfare</a><br /> <br /> I know that it's basically for Vampire: The Masquerade but I used it for my Werewolf: the Apocalypse/Mage: the Ascension crossover chronicle and it worked pretty good.<br /> <br /> There's also an interesting idea in Giovanni Chronicles IV, in which an underground fighting club is depicted, where some of the fighters are supernatural. Ok, just one, a dhampyr if I remember correctly but still imagine The possibilities <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-28-2018, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T14:48:35-07:00","id":1263259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177363-advice-on-how-to-make-a-sadistic-wrestilng-promoter-a-good-villain-for-changelings?p=1177466#post1177466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides Trolls, i wonder which Kith would be best for fighting against a pro wrestler?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean within the rules of the sport, Sluagh. Read their birthright, holding them is almost impossible. A Sluagh who is pinned will simply crawl out from underneath their opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T10:41:17-07:00","id":1264449,"title":"","content":"You know, I just now remembered that there was an episode of Lost Girl which specifically dealt with a problem like this. One of the Fae was some kind of frog creature who secreted a drug that acted like a super steroid.<br /> <br /> If a human took some of this stuff, they would temporarily become strong enough to beat the crap out of an Ogre. But the downside is that prolonged usage would often lead to fatal consequences.<br /> <br /> Anyways, said frog creature was secretly lacing the water bottle of their favored wrestler with the drug, giving them a supernatural edge in the fight.<br /> <br /> I don't fully remember all the details, but I think the frog thing was actually a kid who didn't know about the more fatal aspects of his ability. He was just a devoted fan who wanted to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-04T23:14:13-08:00","id":1264694,"title":"","content":"You could make him a human entertainment Billionaire! Billionaires are fun, they can buy Cyborgs and Submarines!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}